      "side": 1,
      "message": "At default, there is a 15K pull-down resistor on both GPH5/GPH6 pins (on bip board, these two pins are connected to PPC\u0027s INT pin)\nThis issue has been addressed in CL:\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/1105689\n\nThis issue can be reproduced after EC triggers a software reset (eg: wake system up from hibernate or console command \"reboot\").\nThis is becaus 15K pull-down is enabled and USB clock is disabled after the reset.\nAnd the control register of pull-down resistor is belong to the USB module.\nSo we need to ensure USB clock is enabled before setting the control register.",
